PART 2. EXCEPTIONS: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
===================================

The paths below are derived from SigLA: The Signs of Linear A. SigLA is
licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The ShareAlike term reaches derivatives, and the
SigLA manifest states that measurements computed from SigLA material are
derivative work. These paths therefore carry CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, not CC BY 4.0.

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).
Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Required credit line, to travel with any of these paths and with any
derivative of them:

  Sign drawings from SigLA: The Signs of Linear A, a palaeographical
  database, by Ester Salgarella and Simon Castellan
  (https://sigla.phis.me/), licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

Obligations: give credit, link the licence, and state changes (BY); no
commercial use (NC); release derivatives under the same licence (SA); add no
further restrictions.

2.1 SigLA-derived data files
----------------------------

  linear_a/data/sources/sigla/**

    Every file under this path. It includes corpus_structured.json, a
    structured copy of the SigLA corpus.

  linear_a/data/sources/sigla/filemaker_export/**

    The FileMaker exports: fm_decode.csv, fm_doc.csv, fm_role_count.csv,
    fm_summary.csv, fm_role_count.md, fm_summary.md. These are reshaped
    exports of the SigLA structured corpus. The build script fm_ingest.py in
    the same folder is our own code under part 1.

Each of these folders also carries its own LICENSE file, so that a reader who
lands on a deep path sees the terms without reading this file.

2.2 SigLA-provenance records inside a mixed file
------------------------------------------------

  linear_a/data/corpus.json

    This file is a merge of several sources. It is not wholly NC-SA and it is
    not wholly CC BY. The split is machine-readable, by field:

      A record is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 when its "sources" array contains the
      string "sigla". Every such record also carries a "sigla_id" field.

      A record is CC BY 4.0 when its "sources" array does not contain
      "sigla".

    On 2026-09-18 that rule marks 772 of 1,884 records as CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
    Within an NC-SA record, the SigLA-derived fields are "sigla_id",
    "signs" (per-position "type", "role", "reading" and "certain"),
    "sign_count", "scribe", "parent_object" and "face_count".

  linear_a/data/signs.json

    Sign occurrence and document counts are computed over the merged corpus,
    which includes the 772 SigLA records. They are derivative measurements
    under the SigLA ShareAlike term, so this file is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

  linear_a/data/sources/intermediate/unified_corpus_v2.json

    An earlier merge of the same sources. The same field rule applies: a
    record is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 when its "sources" array contains "sigla". On
    2026-09-18 that is 772 of 1,880 records.

  linear_a/data/sources/intermediate/canonical_id_map.json

    The 772 entries that carry a "sigla_id" field tie a SigLA id to a
    canonical document id. Those entries are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The rest of the
    file is CC BY 4.0.

2.3 Image folders (reserved)
----------------------------

No image file is tracked in this repository today. When the SigLA-derived
image layers are published, they land at the paths below and each one carries
the same CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 terms and the credit line above, plus its own LICENSE
file:

  images/sigla/**        SigLA tracings and crops
  images/signs/**        sign exemplar and occurrence crops
  images/documents/**    per-document image sets
  images/a301/**         sign *301 attestation crops
  data/signs/**          per-sign data built from the crops
  data/sigla-merge.json  the SigLA merge table


PART 3. MATERIAL THAT IS NOT LICENSED HERE
==========================================

Some third-party material is cited in this repository but not included in it.
No licence in this file grants any right over it. See CREDITS.md.

  GORILA (Godart and Olivier, 1976 to 1985) and RILA Supplement 1 (Del Freo
  and Zurbach, 2024): cited as sources. No page scan and no text of either
  work is included.

  Photographs and facsimiles from the lineara.xyz mirror: image rights are
  largely Ecole francaise d'Athenes. Not included.

  INSCRIBE 3D models (Universita di Bologna): linked only, not included.

  The PDF library in the private companion repository: copyright of the
  original authors and publishers. Not included.

Public-domain and CC0 upstream material used by the map layer (Natural Earth,
Wikidata, NASA Blue Marble) is credited in CREDITS.md. Copernicus DEM GLO-30
requires an attribution line, which CREDITS.md carries verbatim.
